7` is legal for `RUN_LOOP` but `use_generated(7)` hits `default:`.\n- Added `tests/stdout_parity.rs`: return-value comparison alone would have missed a divergence in any of the three `printf` format strings, since the `driver` binary recompiles the modules rather than loading the `cdylib`.\n- Covered `argc == 0` (NULL `argv[0]` into `printf(\"%s\")`) via `execve` from `pre_exec` — glibc renders it as the empty string, not `\"(null)\"`.\n\n### Two harness bugs I had to fix (worth knowing)\n- `cargo test` does **not** reliably re-emit the `cdylib` on a feature change, so testing without a preceding `cargo build` silently compares a **stale** `.so`. `run_all_configs.sh` builds first, and `load_pair` now hard-fails on a mismatched artifact.\n- Tests clobbering the process-global `G_OP` raced with tests reading it (`dlopen` is refcounted → same mapping), so those moved to their own test binary.\n\nNegative controls confirm the suite isn't vacuously green: swapping in a wrong-`REPEAT` or wrong-`OP` C reference fails 3–15 tests as appropriate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":964,"cache_read_input_tokens":197168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":964,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd9b559f-edbd-4f85-b56b-b12f988f42cb","uuid":"c78addca-3521-4cdf-95c7-b0903ae46b0f","timestamp":"2026-08-29T14:45:36.601Z"}
